.TH sam-jail-repair 1 2026-11-16 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail\-repair \- Repair an app that does not start or misbehaves: list steps, apply one, or undo
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail repair\fR [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-next\fR] [\fB\-\-undo\fR] [\fB\-\-undo\-step\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIAPP\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Repair an app that does not start or misbehaves: list steps, apply one, or undo
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR \fI<APPLY>\fR
Apply the step with this id (see the list)
.TP
\fB\-\-next\fR
Apply the first step in the list
.TP
\fB\-\-undo\fR
Restore the profile from before the first repair step
.TP
\fB\-\-undo\-step\fR \fI<UNDO_STEP>\fR
Switch off one applied repair step (by id), keeping the others
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIAPP\fR>

